OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`.
That path is NOT a project.yml source group and does not exist in this repo. The
repo's real, compiled canonical admin-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/
Admin/**` — where every sibling P7 admin page ships (ApiPlayground, DiskForecast,
SchemaDrift, FleetTelemetryCoverage, LiveSignalInspector, TeslaOrders) and which
`Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups).
The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful
equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Admin`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same
reconciliation every sibling admin-page log recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the admin sub-path `/admin/dlq`. A dedicated
`.dlqInspector` AppRoute case (pathSegment `dlq-inspector`, System group) is added
and `AppRouteParser` maps `/admin/dlq` → `.dlqInspector` via an alias — mirroring
the existing `/admin/schema-drift`→`.schemaDrift` / `/admin/live-signals`→
`.liveSignals` pattern. `DLQInspectorRouteRegistration` hosts the page on
`.dlqInspector` and is wired into the `\.routeHosts` registry chain in
`TeslaSyncApp.swift` (outermost wrapper), so the page is reachable from the
System-group sidebar entry and any `/admin/dlq` deep link.

TYPE REUSE (DRY; avoids same-module ambiguity): the module already owns the
canonical DLQ audit models `DLQReplayResult` (the `RESULT_VARIANT` enum) and
`DLQReplayAuditRecord` (the audit row) in `TeslaSync/feature-views/AuditPanel.Models
.swift` — the native port of the SAME web `admin-diagnostics` contract, and a 1:1
match for this page's audit panel (web `AuditPanel` columns). They are REUSED here
rather than re-declared. The page's own value types (`DLQEntrySummary`,
`DLQEntryFull`, `DLQListReport`, `DLQAuditReport`, `DLQReplayOutcome`) + the
`DLQInspectorDataSource` seam + the `DLQFormat` display formatters live in
`DLQInspectorPageModel.Types.swift`. `AuditResultTone` is mapped onto the shared
`TSTone` at the render edge (`DLQResultBadge.tsTone`). DLQ byte counts are
control-plane (NOT SI-bearing), so — like the sibling DiskForecast page — they
format with binary units at the display boundary and need no SI conversion.

